# OFLIT Child Time Limit — per-weekday daily limit overrides
#
# Overrides are optional. A user with no section here uses the single
# daily limit from /etc/child-time-limit.conf on every weekday, which
# is the behaviour of every release before weekday support.
#
# Manage this file with the CLI; you should not need to edit it by hand:
#
#   child-time set USER DURATION --day DAY   # override one weekday
#   child-time set USER DURATION             # change the base limit
#   child-time limits USER                   # inspect the effective policy
#
# Format
# ------
#   DAYS=SECONDS
#
# DAYS accepts the same weekday expressions as child-time-schedule.conf
# (fri | mon-fri | sat,sun | weekend | daily ...). Every weekday the
# expression selects takes SECONDS as that day's total daily limit.
#
# Example — 1 hour on most days (from child-time-limit.conf) but
# 2 hours on Friday:
#
# [azzahra]
# fri=7200
#
# Rules:
# - A weekday override must be greater than zero.
# - A weekday override must not be below the total scheduled quota of
#   that same weekday.
# - A weekday may be listed only once per user.
